WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:13.350
[Music]

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.600
We've probably got an anniversary
of 50 years next year of growing.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.200
We're second generation.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.000
We currently have a third generation
on board, which is pretty encouraging.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.680
- Yeah, we've got a fair bit of work
  ahead of us, I think.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.520
- We're thinning.
- And no backpackers.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.800
- No, that's going to be the challenge:
  our staffing levels at the moment.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:45.800
I think generally farming is probably
something that's in your blood.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.400
I always had a passion from a young age
to grow stuff.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:54.800
I've done nothing else but grow fruit.
I've lived where I currently live

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.400
for about 49 or 50 years
of my 52 years of life.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:06.080
You get into a situation where it's not
a forced situation. It's a good lifestyle.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.000
The only problem is the amount of hours
you work a week.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.600
We do 60 hours as a quiet week,
and 80's not uncommon.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.400
Since Gavin and I have been in business
together, which is 26, 27 years,

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.900
we've probably achieved what

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.800
two generations do
in our time frame together.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:32.800
We've built a pretty big pack house.
We've got a fair-sized business happening.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.600
It's been a lot of work,
and we haven't necessarily always had,

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.500
as we always put it, old money
to help you along the way.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.000
It's been sink or swim,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.720
and we've been swimming pretty hard.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.800
Well, we used to grow a lot of cherries
years ago,

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.760
and just through
the cherry association meetings,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:05.600
Tom was always there and in our ear:
"Give me a go, give me a go."

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:12.130
It would be 14, 15, 16 years,
something like that,

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:18.690
since we first gave him a try on one block
that was struggling a little bit.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:24.640
Now we use Hybrid Ag fertilisers
across the whole farm.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:34.000
[Music]
